config INOTIFY_USER
	bool "Inotify support for userspace"
	select FSNOTIFY
	default y
	help
	  Say Y here to enable inotify support for userspace, including the
	  associated system calls.  Inotify allows monitoring of both files and
	  directories via a single open fd.  Events are read from the file
	  descriptor, which is also select()- and poll()-able.
	  Inotify fixes numerous shortcomings in dnotify and introduces several
	  new features including multiple file events, one-shot support, and
	  unmount notification.

	  For more information, see <file:Documentation/filesystems/inotify.rst>

	  If unsure, say Y.

config RUST_INOTIFY_USER
	bool "Rust inotify userspace implementation"
	depends on RUST && INOTIFY_USER
	help
	  Build inotify_user.o from its Rust translation. Watch descriptors,
	  user event delivery, syscalls, group allocation and initialization
	  are implemented in Rust. Configured kernel macro, header-inline and
	  syscall declaration boundaries use a dedicated C helper object.
	  The original C provider remains available when this option is off.
